# La foresta, capitolo 1 (forest/forest_zone.gd). Un cue per cosa con cui si parla (il
# nome del tile), più arrive (l'atterraggio) ed exit (l'uscita della zona).

~ arrive
Grass. Cold, wet grass, under her cheek.
Above her, leaves. So many leaves the sky is only a few holes of light.
Trees everywhere. Taller than the house. Taller than anything.
Lethe: ...Where...?
Something sharp is still in her hand. A piece of the mirror.
It doesn't hurt yet.
=> END

# Selene scende dalla luna (forest_zone.gd, meet_selene): la prima scelta del capitolo.
# La verità accende la magia (learn_truth); la bugia no, ma la spada la sente.
~ selene_meet
A light comes down through the leaves. Small, curved. Like a piece of the moon.
It stops in front of her face. It hums.
Selene: Oh. You're awake. Good.
Selene: I'm Selene. I came down from your window. The moon in it.
Lethe: ...My window?
Selene: I've been watching your room for a long time. Every night, the same night.
Selene: Are you hurt?
- I'm fine.
	Lethe: I'm fine. [#wrong]
	set lies += 1
	Selene: ...Okay. If you say so.
	The glass in her hand catches the light. Like it heard her.
- My hand. The glass cut me.
	Lethe: My hand. The glass... it cut me.
	set truth += 1
	do learn_truth()
	Something warm opens in her palm. Not glass. Light.
	Selene: See? When you say it, it shines.
Selene: Come on. There's a path. I'll stay close.
=> END

~ mirror
if seen("mirror") == 0
	A small mirror, standing alone in the grass. A violet frame, like her dress.
	It reflects the moon. Not her.
	Lethe: Same glass as the one in my room...
	if selene_met()
		Selene: You can rest here. The glass remembers you.
		Selene: If you fall... you'll wake up in front of it. I promise.
else
	The moon in the mirror hasn't moved.
She rests a moment, close to the glass. Her heart loosens.
do rest()
=> END

# Quando il cuore è stretto del tutto (forest_zone.gd, die): si riparte dallo specchio.
~ wake_again
Lethe: ...
The mirror is cold against her back. She's still here.
if selene_met()
	Selene: You're back. ...You're back.
	Selene: Don't do that again. Please.
	- I'm okay.
		Lethe: I'm okay. [#wrong]
		set lies += 1
	- That hurt.
		Lethe: That hurt. A lot.
		set truth += 1
		Selene: I know. I felt it too.
=> END

~ brambles
Thorns, grown thick across the path. [shiver]Something glints behind them.[/shiver]
Lethe: I can't get through. ...Not like this.
if selene_met() and seen("brambles") == 0
	Selene: They grew shut. Like curtains nobody opens.
	Selene: Maybe someday you'll know how to open them.
=> END

~ old_stone
An old stone with a mark carved in it. It glows, a little.
Lethe: An eye. Or a moon.
if selene_met()
	Selene: ...Someone was here before you.
	Selene: They didn't go back.
=> END

# Il primo nemico (forest_story.gd, first_enemy): tutto si ferma, la camera lo guarda.
~ first_enemy
Something moves in the dark between the trees. It has no face.
Lethe: ...That's the dark from under my bed.
Selene: Careful. It's not a moth. Not really. It's made of the things you didn't say.
if knows("truth_spark")
	Selene: You have the light, and the glass. Light is slower. Glass cuts both ways.
else
	Selene: You have the glass. Use it if you have to.
	Selene: It will want you to.
=> END

# Il ruscello del Lete. Con Selene: la sua prima bugia ("just a sip"), e una seconda
# occasione per la prima verità (se a Selene Lethe ha mentito, la magia arriva qui).
~ lethe
Black water, very still. It doesn't reflect anything.
It smells like sleep.
if not selene_met()
	Lethe: ...I'm not thirsty. [#wrong]
elif seen("lethe") == 0
	Selene: That's the Lethe. It runs through everything here.
	Selene: Just a sip. It stops hurting. [#wrong]
	- I'm not thirsty.
		Lethe: ...I'm not thirsty. [#wrong]
		set lies += 1
		Selene: ...Right. Neither am I.
	- It scares me.
		Lethe: It scares me. It's too quiet.
		set truth += 1
		do learn_truth()
		Selene: ...Yeah. Me too, a little.
else
	The water doesn't move. Selene stays close to her shoulder.
=> END

~ exit
The path goes on, deeper into the trees.
Somewhere ahead, something is white. Like bone. Like a dead tree.
if selene_met()
	Selene: ...There. Can you feel it? Something up ahead is very tired.
	Lethe: It looks like the plant on my windowsill.
	Selene: Then it's waiting for you.
=> END
